    "fields": "pk = mldsa65PK(1952) || P-384 point (97, SEC1 uncompressed); sk = mldsa65Seed(32) || ECPrivateKey (RFC 5915 DER, 64 bytes: the 48-byte scalar sits at offset 7, then the secp384r1 OID); s signs m with an empty context, sWithContext with ctx; each signature is mldsa65Sig(3309) || ECDSA-with-SHA-384 as DER Ecdsa-Sig-Value (variable length). Both halves are randomized upstream (ML-DSA hedged, ECDSA not RFC 6979), so these signatures are pinned by VERIFYING, never by re-producing them. sWithContext's ECDSA half happens to have a HIGH s: valid under the draft, refused by Kryptolog's verifiers, which require low-S (see test/hybrid.test.js).",
